## Item 2 — Full FDA disclaimer in the website footer

Requested verbatim text:

```
The statements made regarding these products have not been evaluated
by the Food and Drug Administration. The efficacy of these products
has not been confirmed by FDA-approved research. These products are
not intended to diagnose, treat, cure, or prevent any disease
```

**Implementation:** added as the canonical `nav_get_disclaimer('fda')`
string in `inc/compliance.php` (single-sourced, like the RUO line) and
rendered as a second paragraph directly under the sitewide RUO
disclaimer in the footer (`footer.php`). Both disclaimers coexist: the
RUO line remains on all its existing surfaces and in the JSON-LD
`disambiguatingDescription`, satisfying the processor's scanner
cross-check; the FDA text is footer-only, as requested.

⚠️ The FDA string intentionally contains "diagnose / treat / cure /
prevent" — terms banned everywhere else on the site (see
`docs/COMPLIANCE` → Prohibited Language). They are permitted ONLY
inside this canonical disclaimer. Do not edit, paraphrase, or scrub it.

## Item 3 — Remove Mastercard card-brand logo from footer

**Implementation:** the `'mastercard'` entry in the footer payment-marks
array (`footer.php`) is commented out, not deleted; the SVG asset stays
in the repo (`assets/images/payments/mastercard.svg`) but is no longer
rendered. Do not re-enable without processor sign-off. Other brand
marks (Visa, Amex, Discover, crypto, ACH) were not flagged.

## Item 4 — Checkout must REQUIRE account creation

Guest checkout is not allowed; an account must exist before an order
can be placed.

**Implementation:** enforced in code via `pre_option_*` filters in
`inc/woocommerce.php` (not wp-admin Accounts & Privacy settings, so a
settings edit on prod can never silently re-enable guest checkout):

- `woocommerce_enable_guest_checkout` → forced `no`
- `woocommerce_enable_signup_and_login_from_checkout` → forced `yes`
- `woocommerce_enable_checkout_login_reminder` → forced `yes`
- `woocommerce_registration_generate_username` → forced `yes`
  (username derived from billing email — "nothing too detailed")
- `woocommerce_registration_generate_password` → forced `no`
  (checkout always shows a visible required "Create account password"
  field; with both generation options on, WooCommerce hides the account
  section and creates accounts silently, which would not read as
  "account required" to a processor reviewer)

The RUO acknowledgment checkbox requirement is unchanged and was
verified to still render alongside the account fields.
